# Legacy CDN media passphrase — template. Committed; the real file is not.
#
# Copy this to `media.properties` (gitignored) and put the passphrase after
# the `=`. It is read at build time into BuildConfig.MEDIA_PASSPHRASE and
# decrypts the doha ciphertext downloaded from apt.vridhamma.org.
#
#     cp media.properties.example media.properties
#     # then edit media.properties and paste the passphrase
#
# To avoid leaving it in your shell history, prefer an editor over `echo`.
# If you must use the shell, a leading space keeps it out of history on a
# default bash/zsh setup:
#
#      printf 'niyam.mediaPassphrase=%s\n' 'THE-PASSPHRASE' > media.properties
#
# Verify without revealing it — the build prints presence only:
#
#     ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug | grep "media key"
#
# Rules (docs/… and AGENTS.md "Media key"):
#   - never commit it, never log it, never show it in the UI
#   - a build with no key is valid: Sounds shows the no-media-key state and
#     downloads stay disabled. Do not "fix" that by hardcoding a default.

niyam.mediaPassphrase=
